## 3. Investigations

### IR verification of the bfp4 MLP override (skill section A)
- The override is confirmed applied at both the config level and the TTNN IR level.
- Config level: run3 `non-default args` log shows
  `weight_dtype_overrides='.../overrides_qwen05b_mlp_bfp4.json'` in additional_config,
  and NO "did not match any model parameters" warning was emitted (glob matched).
- TTNN IR level: compared the largest prefill graph ttnn IR (`modules/irs/ttnn_...g6_*.mlir`)
  run2 (no override) vs run3 (bfp4 MLP):
  - run2: `bfp_bf4` = 1 (an enum legend only), `bfp_bf8` = 2314, `bf16` = 6939.
  - run3: `bfp_bf4` = 869, `bfp_bf8` = 1786, `bf16` = 6939.
  => ~528 bfp_bf8 tensor uses migrated to bfp_bf4, i.e. the 72 MLP {gate,up,down}_proj
     weights (and their downstream tiles) are now bf4 while the rest stay bf8. Override
     verified real, not silently dropped.
- Param-name confidence: glob `model.layers.*.mlp.*proj.weight` matched exactly 72
  params via `named_parameters()` (24 layers × {gate,up,down}); all end in `.weight`.

